# ── Dungeon Tracker icons ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Draws the app's own icon set (instead of emoji) and writes src/icons.svg (an SVG sprite of <symbol id="i-<name>">)
# and src/icons.json (emoji → icon name). Run: python3 tools/gen-icons.py . (tools/build.js inlines both into the web
# pages; web/icons.js swaps emoji in the page for these icons as the page draws).
# Style: a 24×24 grid, round 1.8 strokes in currentColor (like the outline dice) plus a soft accent fill in
# var(--ia) (the theme's brass, see web/icons.css) for depth. They scale with the text (1em), so the same symbols
# work at 16 px in a button and at 100 px in the roll animations.
#   a() accent fill shape · s() stroke path · f() solid currentColor · ca/cs/cf the same for circles
# To add one: draw it in I, add its emoji to MAP, run this script, check tools/../icons preview if you like.
# (var(--ia), the theme's brass) for depth. a() = accent fill shape, s() = stroke path, f() = solid currentColor fill.
A='style="fill:var(--ia,currentColor);fill-opacity:var(--iao,.3);stroke:none"'
F='fill="currentColor" stroke="none"'
def a(d): return f'<path {A} d="{d}"/>'
def s(d): return f'<path d="{d}"/>'
def f(d): return f'<path {F} d="{d}"/>'
def ca(cx,cy,r): return f'<circle {A} cx="{cx}" cy="{cy}" r="{r}"/>'
def cs(cx,cy,r): return f'<circle cx="{cx}" cy="{cy}" r="{r}"/>'
def cf(cx,cy,r): return f'<circle {F} cx="{cx}" cy="{cy}" r="{r}"/>'
